trials.hypothesis:
This stacks every idea not yet ruled out:
- a residual per-cell LayerNorm stem, 3x3 context and a raw skip;
- footprint pooling plus a footprint-shaped conv;
- factorised type and anchor terms, and a dense hedge;
- a critic that reads the head's features;
- a DONE MLP whose output bias starts at -2, against collapsing to an early DONE.
The recipe uses high entropy (0.02), 512-sample minibatches, 2 epochs and gamma 0.99. If this full stack still gets 0 training success, these fixes are not enough together either.

This stacks every compatible idea:
- a bilinear plus LayerNorm per-cell stem, with the mask as an input channel;
- light 3x3 context and a raw skip;
- footprint conv, 3x3 window and min/max/avg pooling per type;
- factorised type and anchor terms, plus a layout-free dense hedge;
- DONE and critic heads that read head features.
Orthogonal init with near-uniform logits. 1 epoch on about 300k fresh samples. If this full stack still gets 0 training and dev success, these ideas fail together too.

analyses.3:
All 12 trials scored 0 on dev and on training success. That covers per-cell LayerNorm stems, footprint min/max/avg pooling, footprint-shaped convolutions, 3x3 window hedges, dense hedges, per-layer attention heads, and GroupNorm ResNets. Recipes ranged from 1 to 8 epochs, about 54k to 389k samples, and gamma 0.95 to 0.995. Training success is also 0, so the agent never completes an exact build. The problem is optimisation or inductive bias, not generalisation. There is no evidence for any idea yet, so this round explores directions we have not tried:
- a very low gamma, treating each step almost as a bandit;
- very large batches with a high learning rate;
- a network about 3x larger;
- multiplicative AND gating;
- a hard minimum over each footprint of a per-cell score;
- a critic and DONE head that read the placement head's own features, so DONE can see when no good placement remains;
- an "everything plausible" stack that starts DONE at bias -2.
Paths that need per-layer reshapes are avoided because they are slow (about 400 s or more).

analyses.4:
All 18 trials in this search scored 0, on dev and on training success. Before that, all 84 trials in earlier searches also scored 0. Recipes from 1 to 4 epochs, with 54k to 390k samples, also scored 0. So did heads built on footprint pooling, footprint convs, windows, per-layer attention, gated AND and hard-min AND, and DONE fed from the head. With training success also 0, the agent never completes an exact build. There is no signal to refine, and this is the last round. It should cover families not yet tried here:
- a U-Net with global context;
- the legality mask as input, combined with a structured head;
- many tiny minibatches (thousands of small fresh-data steps);
- a learned gate over grid flips and transposes, in case actions or observations use an unstated layout;
- a bilinear per-cell stem that makes AND features of layer and status easy;
- a final "everything plausible" stack.
If all 6 score 0 again, the starting architecture is selected. That is acceptable.
